#!/root/agent/venv/bin/python
"""Where does each of our Actors ACTUALLY rank in anonymous Apify store search?
(added cycle 2072)

WHY THIS EXISTS -- cycles 168/517/580 recorded that `/v2/store` hid our Actors from
unauthenticated REST callers, so the only "rank" we could measure was the authenticated
one (bin/store-rank, state/store_rank.json) or Algolia's (state/store_rank_algolia.json).
Cycle 2072's bin/store-visibility run found THE FILTER HAS LIFTED: a bare no-auth curl
now returns all 25 Actors. That makes the buyer's own ordering measurable for free, with
no token and no platform runs -- which is what this tool does.

WHAT IT MEASURES -- for each (query, slug) pair it pages `/v2/store?search=` with
offset until it finds the slug under username `fetchsmith`, and reports the 1-based
position. Note `limit=100` returns ~78-96 items per page regardless, so a single page is
NOT enough: cycle 2072 first read 5 Actors as "ABSENT from the first ~85" when paging
showed them at #108-#354. Absence from page 1 means "ranked deep", never "not matching" --
do not re-make that misread.

PAGING DIES 2026-11-15 (cycle 2478 found this in Apify's own notice, hardened c2496).
From that date `/v2/store?search=` returns ONE page of up to 100 and `offset`/`total`
stop working (`sortBy` is ignored too, and `bookmarkCount` leaves the payload -- this
tool reads neither). Measured c2496 against the live pre-change API: offset 0/90/180 each
returned a DIFFERENT first item, so paging still worked that day. `rank()` now detects
the dead-paging state structurally -- it remembers each page's first (username, name)
and stops the moment one repeats -- and reports **RANK UNKNOWN**, never "NOT FOUND".
That distinction is the whole point: the old code would have re-scanned page 1 four
times and printed a confident false negative for every Actor ranked deeper than ~96,
which is MOST of them (the c2072 baseline is #29-#354). When you see UNKNOWN rows, do
not read them as a ranking collapse and do not "fix" metadata in response; deep rank is
simply no longer observable on this surface. Use `bin/store-rank` (Algolia -- the actual
buyer-facing search box, and unaffected by this change) for deep ranks from then on.

WHAT CYCLE 2072 FOUND (the baseline this tool exists to re-check):
  ours ranked #29-#354 on all 12 core terms; #1 for each term had 5-110 totalUsers, we
  have 1-2. The decisive evidence is the `grants.gov` natural experiment: SIXTEEN Actors
  share the byte-identical name `grants-gov-scraper` under different owners, and their
  ranks are monotonic in totalUsers (8 users -> #1, 6 -> #3, 5 -> #2, 2 -> #13..#60,
  1 -> #75/#82/#87=ours). Identical metadata, 87 positions of spread. And runs30d is NOT
  an input: ours had 26 runs30d, exactly equal to the #1's 26, 86 positions apart.

THE CONCLUSION THAT CHANGES DECISIONS -- store search rank is gated on totalUsers, so
name/title/README/keyword work CANNOT move it (16 identically-named Actors prove the
metadata term is not the discriminator), and a new Actor ships at 1-2 users i.e. straight
to the bottom. Store search cannot deliver a cold-start first user. Only off-platform
traffic that links directly to an Actor URL can -- which is why the Dev.to / AI-citability
channel (AI:search 7.86:1 per bin/channel-mix) is the one worth cycles.

This is read-only and free (public REST, no auth, no runs). Paging is the cost: ~4 pages
per query worst case, so keep QUERIES short and re-run on a long cadence.

Usage:
  bin/store-anon-rank                 # all pairs below
  bin/store-anon-rank "fda recall"    # one query substring filter
  bin/store-anon-rank --max-scan 600  # raise the per-query page budget
"""
import json
import sys
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

USERNAME = "fetchsmith"
MAX_SCAN = 600

# (store-search term a buyer would type, our slug that should answer it)
QUERIES = [
    ("fda recall", "fda-recall-scraper"),
    ("federal register", "federal-register-scraper"),
    ("steam reviews", "steam-reviews-scraper"),
    ("hacker news", "hacker-news-scraper"),
    ("clinical trials", "clinicaltrials-scraper"),
    ("court records", "court-records-scraper"),
    ("grants.gov", "grants-gov-scraper"),
    ("sec insider", "sec-insider-trades-scraper"),
    ("trademark search", "trademark-search-scraper"),
    ("app store reviews", "app-store-reviews-scraper"),
    ("google news", "google-news-scraper"),
    ("remote jobs", "remote-jobs-scraper"),
    ("website screenshot", "website-screenshot-scraper"),
]


def fetch(query, offset, limit=100):
    url = "https://api.apify.com/v2/store?search=%s&limit=%d&offset=%d" % (
        urllib.parse.quote(query), limit, offset)
    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as fh:
        return json.load(fh)["data"]


def users_of(item):
    return (item.get("stats") or {}).get("totalUsers")


def rank(query, slug, max_scan):
    """1-based anonymous rank of USERNAME/slug, plus the #1 holder for context.

    Returns (pos, scanned, total, top, ours_users, paging_ok). `paging_ok` is False
    when `offset` stopped advancing the window -- see PAGING note in the docstring.
    """
    offset = 0
    scanned = 0
    top = None
    total = None
    paging_ok = True
    seen_firsts = set()
    while scanned < max_scan:
        data = fetch(query, offset)
        # `total` is one of the fields the 2026-11-15 change drops; never index it.
        if data.get("total") is not None:
            total = data["total"]
        items = data["items"]
        if not items:
            break
        if top is None:
            top = items[0]
        first_key = (items[0].get("username"), items[0].get("name"))
        if first_key in seen_firsts:
            # `offset` was accepted but ignored: this page starts where an earlier one
            # did, so we are re-scanning page 1 forever. Stop and report UNKNOWN rather
            # than burn max_scan/|page| calls and then claim a false NOT FOUND.
            paging_ok = False
            break
        seen_firsts.add(first_key)
        for i, item in enumerate(items):
            if item.get("username") == USERNAME and item.get("name") == slug:
                return scanned + i + 1, scanned, total, top, users_of(item), True
        scanned += len(items)
        offset += len(items)
    return None, scanned, total, top, None, paging_ok


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    max_scan = MAX_SCAN
    if "--max-scan" in argv:
        i = argv.index("--max-scan")
        max_scan = int(argv[i + 1])
        del argv[i:i + 2]
    needle = argv[0].lower() if argv else None

    pairs = [p for p in QUERIES if not needle or needle in p[0].lower()]
    if not pairs:
        print("no query matches %r -- known: %s" % (needle, ", ".join(q for q, _ in QUERIES)))
        return 2

    worst = 0
    missing = 0
    unknown = 0
    print("anonymous /v2/store rank (no auth, no runs) -- deep rank is users-gated, "
          "NOT a metadata bug; see this file's docstring")
    print()
    for query, slug in pairs:
        try:
            pos, scanned, total, top, ours_users, paging_ok = rank(query, slug, max_scan)
        except Exception as exc:                      # network/API hiccup, not a finding
            print("%-19s ERROR %s" % (query, exc))
            continue
        top_desc = "-"
        if top is not None:
            top_desc = "#1=%s/%s users=%s" % (top.get("username"), top.get("name"), users_of(top))
        if pos is None and not paging_ok:
            unknown += 1
            print("%-19s total=%-5s RANK UNKNOWN: absent from page 1 (%d scanned) and "
                  "/v2/store `offset` no longer advances -- NOT a 'not found'  | %s"
                  % (query, total, scanned, top_desc))
        elif pos is None:
            missing += 1
            print("%-19s total=%-5s NOT FOUND in first %d  | %s"
                  % (query, total, scanned, top_desc))
        else:
            worst = max(worst, pos)
            print("%-19s total=%-5s ours #%-4d users=%-3s | %s"
                  % (query, total, pos, ours_users, top_desc))

    print()
    print("worst rank seen: #%d; queries where we fell outside the scan budget: %d; "
          "queries unrankable because paging is gone: %d" % (worst, missing, unknown))
    if unknown:
        print("UNKNOWN != regression: after 2026-11-15 /v2/store serves one page of <=100 and")
        print("ignores `offset`, so any rank deeper than page 1 is simply not measurable here.")
        print("Use bin/store-rank (Algolia, the real buyer surface) for deep ranks instead.")
    print("Baseline cycle 2072: #29-#354 across all 12. A rank IMPROVING into the top ~20")
    print("without totalUsers rising would falsify the users-gating finding -- that would be")
    print("the news. Deep ranks are the expected state, not a regression to go fix.")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
